arse_lines (this, lines, n_lines, status, errors) In-memory sibling of schema_parse : validate + apply a namelist\nalready held as a lines(:) character array (no file touch).\nSame error-return convention as schema_parse . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( nml_schema_t ), intent(inout) :: this character(len=*), intent(in) :: lines (:) integer, intent(in) :: n_lines integer, intent(out), optional :: status character(len=:), intent(out), optional, allocatable :: errors (:) procedure, public :: render_json => schema_render_json private  subroutine schema_render_json (this, path) Emit the schema as JSON: one object per group, nesting one object\nper key.  This is the ONLY thing tools/gen_python_config.py reads – it parses no Fortran source, mirroring the precedent schema_render_markdown already set for docs/generated_nml_knobs.md . &ocean_bc_nml is NOT here – it is registered via add_external_group (see rdb_config.F90 ), so it carries no keys\non this schema; python/rdb/_config_bc.py is a hand-written\nstub with its own drift test (see docs D5.7). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( nml_schema_t ), intent(in) :: this character(len=*), intent(in) :: path procedure, public :: render_markdown => schema_render_markdown private  subroutine schema_render_markdown (this, path) Render the schema as Markdown: per group a heading, doc line,\nand a knob table. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( nml_schema_t ), intent(in) :: this character(len=*), intent(in) :: path procedure, public :: write_doc_all => schema_write_doc_all private  subroutine schema_write_doc_all (this, path) Write every group and key as valid namelist with aligned docs. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( nml_schema_t ), intent(in) :: this character(len=*), intent(in) :: path procedure, public :: write_doc_short => schema_write_doc_short private  subroutine schema_write_doc_short (this, path) Write only non-default keys (MOM6 parameter_doc