ment that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: i integer, private :: j Source Code pure subroutine ice_tau_mirror_impl ( tau_ocn_x , tau_ocn_y , tau_x , tau_y , nx , ny ) !! PR 63. Device copy of the blend's OUTPUT into the restart-carried !! mirror fields — deliberately NOT fused into !! `ice_ocean_stress_flux_impl` (that kernel stays untouched so the !! `tau_coupling` bitwise gate is unaffected by this PR). !! Explicit-shape + decl-order (integer dims before the arrays that !! use them). integer , intent ( in ) :: nx , ny real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: tau_ocn_x ( nx + 1 , ny ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: tau_ocn_y ( nx , ny + 1 ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: tau_x ( nx + 1 , ny ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: tau_y ( nx , ny + 1 ) integer :: i , j do concurrent ( j = 1 : ny , i = 1 : nx + 1 ) tau_ocn_x ( i , j ) = tau_x ( i , j ) end do do concurrent ( j = 1 : ny + 1 , i = 1 : nx ) tau_ocn_y ( i , j ) = tau_y ( i , j ) end do end subroutine ice_tau_mirror_impl","tags":"","url":"proc/ice_tau_mirror_impl.html"},{"title":"stress_scratch_ensure – Roundabout","text":"private  subroutine stress_scratch_ensure(nx, ny) Lazily (re)allocate + device-map the per-step tau-blend scratch\n(F6). Size change tears down and rebuilds. Never called inside a\nper-substep loop (this whole coupler runs once per outer step). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nx integer, intent(in) :: ny Calls proc~~stress_scratch_ensure~~CallsGraph proc~stress_scratch_ensure stress_scratch_ensure proc~ice_ocean_stress_cleanup ice_ocean_stress_cleanup proc~stress_scratch_ensure->proc~ice_ocean_stress_cleanup Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the fo