es , wp ) / real ( BYTES_PER_GIB , wp ) str = two_dp ( gib ) // \" GB\" else mib = real ( bytes , wp ) / real ( BYTES_PER_MIB , wp ) str = two_dp ( mib ) // \" MB\" end if end function mem_format_bytes","tags":"","url":"proc/mem_format_bytes.html"},{"title":"mem_host_rss_bytes – Roundabout","text":"public  function mem_host_rss_bytes() result(bytes) Resident set size of the current process, in bytes, parsed from VmRSS in /proc/self/status (reported in kB → scaled to\nbytes).  Returns -1 if the file is unreadable or the field is\nabsent (non-Linux platforms).  Never aborts. Arguments None Return Value integer(kind=int64) Called by proc~~mem_host_rss_bytes~~CalledByGraph proc~mem_host_rss_bytes mem_host_rss_bytes proc~driver_run_ocean driver_run_ocean proc~driver_run_ocean->proc~mem_host_rss_bytes proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_ocean Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial character(len=256), private :: iomsg integer, private :: ios integer(kind=int64), private :: kb character(len=32), private :: kb_str character(len=256), private :: line integer, private :: unit Source Code function mem_host_rss_bytes () result ( bytes ) !! Resident set size of the current process, in bytes, parsed from !! `VmRSS` in `/proc/self/status` (reported in kB → scaled to !! bytes).