ure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~derived_catalog_size~~CalledByGraph proc~derived_catalog_size derived_catalog_size proc~rdb_ocean_derived_catalog_name rdb_ocean_derived_catalog_name proc~rdb_ocean_derived_catalog_name->proc~derived_catalog_size proc~rdb_ocean_derived_catalog_size rdb_ocean_derived_catalog_size proc~rdb_ocean_derived_catalog_size->proc~derived_catalog_size Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code function derived_catalog_size () result ( n ) !! Public only for the unit-test suite. integer :: n call ensure_catalog_initialised () n = N_CATALOG end function derived_catalog_size","tags":"","url":"proc/derived_catalog_size.html"},{"title":"catalog_name_list – Roundabout","text":"private  function catalog_name_list() result(list) Comma-separated list of catalog diagnostic names (for error text). Arguments None Return Value character(len=:), allocatable Calls proc~~catalog_name_list~~CallsGraph proc~catalog_name_list catalog_name_list proc~ensure_catalog_initialised ensure_catalog_initialised proc~catalog_name_list->proc~ensure_catalog_initialised Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~catalog_name_list~~CalledByGraph proc~catalog_name_list catalog_name_list proc~register_derived register_derived proc~register_derived->proc~catalog_name_list proc~apply_diag_selection apply_diag_selection proc~apply_diag_selection->proc~register_derived proc~engine_configure_diag engine_configure_diag proc~engine_configure_diag->proc~apply_diag_selection proc~engine_setup engine_setup proc~engine_setup->proc~engine_configure_diag proc~complete_ocean_create complete_ocean_create proc~complete_ocean_create->proc~engine_setup proc~driver_run_ocean driver_run_ocean proc~driver_run_ocean->proc~engine_setup Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: i Source Code function catalog_name_list () result ( list ) !! Comma-separated list of catalog diagnostic names (for error text). character ( len = :), allocatable :: list integer :: i call ensure_catalog_initialised () list = \"\" do i = 1 , N_CATALOG if ( i > 1 ) list = list // \", \" list = list // trim ( CATALOG ( i )% name ) end do end function catalog_name_list","tags":"","url":"proc/catalog_name_list.html"},{"title":"gate_clause – Roundabout","text":"private pure function gate_clause(name) result(clause) Render canonical_diag_gate_hint(name) into a human-readable\nsentence for the “requested but not registered” warning.  Phrased\nas a QUESTION, never a diagnosis: the hint is a hand-maintained\nmirror of register_default_diags ’s gates (§11.2 of the PR-64\nplan) and can drift from the true cause.  An empty hint means the\ndiagnostic is one of the four unconditional ones (SSH/u/v/KE) and\nSHOULD have registered — that is a bug, not a closed gate. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: name Return Value character(len=96) Calls proc~~gate_clause~~CallsGraph proc~gate_clause gate_clause proc~canonical_diag_gate_hint canonical_diag_gate_hint proc~gate_clause->proc~canonical_diag_gate_hint Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~gate_clause~~CalledByGraph proc~gate_clause gate_clause proc~apply_diag_selection apply_diag_selection proc~apply_diag_selection->proc~gate_clause proc~engine_configure_diag engine_configure_diag proc~engine_configure_diag->proc~apply_diag_selection proc~engine_setup engine_setup proc~engine_setup->proc~engine_configure_diag proc~complete_ocean_create complete_ocean_create proc~complete_ocean_create->proc~engine_setup proc~driver_run_ocean driver_run_ocean proc~driver_run_ocean->proc~engine_setup proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_ocean proc~rdb_ocean_create_finalize rdb_ocean_create_finalize proc~rdb_ocean_create_finalize->proc~complete_ocean_create proc~rdb_ocean_create_from_string rdb_ocean_create_from_string proc~rdb_ocean_create_from_string->proc~complete_ocean_create Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial character(len=64), private :: hint Source Code pure function gate_clause ( name ) result ( clause ) !! Render `canonical_diag_gate_hint(name)` into a human-readable !! sentence for the \"requested but not registered\" warning.  Phrased !! as a QUESTION, never a diagnosis: the hint is a hand-maintained !! mirror of `register_default_diags`'s gates (§11.2 of the PR-64 !! plan) and can drift from the true cause.  An empty hint means the !! diagnostic is one of the four unconditional ones (SSH/u/v/KE) and !! SHOULD have registered — that is a bug, not a closed gate. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name character ( len = 96 ) :: clause character ( len = 64 ) :: hint hint = canonical_diag_gate_hint ( name ) if ( len_trim ( hint ) > 0 ) then clause = \"Is \" // trim ( hint ) // \" off?\" else clause = \"This diagnostic has no feature gate — please report this.\" end if end function gate_clause","tags":"","url":"proc/gate_clause.html"},{"title":"apply_diag_selection – Roundabout","text":"public  subroutine apply_diag_selection(state, spec, dt_out, default_coord) Configure the ocean diagnostic set from the unified &ocean_diag_nml diags selection string.  Single production entry\npoint: parses spec once, registers the canonical defaults\n(consulting the spec for per-diagnostic :off skips and :cadence / :op / :coord overrides), then registers any spec\nentries that name a derived-catalog diagnostic (with their overrides). default_coord (a DIAG_VGRID_* , default LAYER) is the global\noutput vgrid ( &ocean_diag_nml vgrid ) applied to layered diagnostics\nthat don’t carry a per-diag :coord . An empty / blank spec + LAYER default reproduces the canonical set\nexactly (bit-identical).  A spec name that is neither canonical nor\nin the derived catalog fails loud via register_derived .  A :off on a non-canonical name that is not registered is a harmless no-op. Must be called AFTER the output-level setters ( set_output_z_levels / set_output_sigma_levels / set_output_zstar_levels / set_output_density_levels ) so non-layer diagnostics size their\nremap targets correctly. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( ocean_state_t ), intent(inout), target :: state character(len=*), intent(in) :: spec real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: dt_out integer, intent(in), optional :: default_coord Calls proc~~apply_diag_selection~~CallsGraph proc~apply_diag_selection apply_diag_selection proc~gate_clause gate_clause proc~apply_diag_selection->proc~gate_clause proc~is_canonical_diag_name is_canonical_diag_name proc~apply_diag_selection->proc~is_canonical_diag_name proc~ocean_diag_is_registered ocean_diag_t%ocean_diag_is_registered proc~apply_diag_selection->proc~ocean_diag_is_registered proc~parse_diag_spec parse_diag_spec proc~apply_diag_selection->proc~parse_diag_spec proc~register_default_diags register_default_diags proc~apply_diag_selection->proc~register_default_diags proc~register_derived register_derived proc~apply_diag_selection->proc~register_derived warning warning proc~apply_diag_selection->warning proc~canonical_diag_gate_hint canonical_diag_gate_hint proc~gate_clause->proc~canonical_diag_gate_hint proc~parse_one_spec_token parse_one_spec_token proc~parse_diag_spec->proc~parse_one_spec_token proc~register_one_canonical register_one_canonical proc~register_default_diags->proc~register_one_canonical error error proc~register_derived->error proc~catalog_name_list catalog_name_list proc~register_derived->proc~catalog_name_list proc~coord_remap_proc coord_remap_proc proc~register_derived->proc~coord_remap_proc proc~diag_mask_vanished_is_on diag_mask_vanished_is_on proc~register_derived->proc~diag_mask_vanished_is_on proc~ensure_catalog_initialised ensure_catalog_initialised proc~register_derived->proc~ensure_catalog_initialised proc~error_ring_push error_ring_push proc~register_derived->proc~error_ring_push proc~ocean_diag_register ocean_diag_t%ocean_diag_register proc~register_derived->proc~ocean_diag_register proc~catalog_name_list->proc~ensure_catalog_initialised proc~reset_accumulator reset_accumulator proc~ocean_diag_register->proc~reset_accumulator proc~parse_one_spec_token->error proc~lower_ascii lower_ascii proc~parse_one_spec_token->proc~lower_ascii proc~parse_cadence_attr parse_cadence_attr proc~parse_one_spec_token->proc~parse_cadence_attr proc~register_one_canonical->proc~coord_remap_proc proc~register_one_canonical->proc~ocean_diag_register proc~resolve_canonical_spec resolve_canonical_spec proc~register_one_canonical->proc~resolve_canonical_spec proc~fill_buffer_impl fill_buffer_impl proc~reset_accumulator->proc~fill_buffer_impl Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~apply_diag_selection~~CalledByGraph proc~apply_diag_selection apply_diag_selection proc~engine_configure_diag engine_configure_diag proc~engine_configure_diag->proc~apply_diag_selection proc~engine_setup engine_setup proc~engine_setup->proc~engine_configure_diag proc~complete_ocean_create complete_ocean_create proc~complete_ocean_create->proc~engine_setup proc~driver_run_ocean driver_run_ocean proc~driver_run_ocean->proc~engine_setup proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_ocean proc~rdb_ocean_create_finalize rdb_ocean_create_finalize proc~rdb_ocean_create_finalize->proc~complete_ocean_create proc~rdb_ocean_create_from_string rdb_ocean_create_from_string proc~rdb_ocean_create_from_string->proc~complete_ocean_create Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: coord integer, private :: dcoord real(kind=wp), private :: dto real(kind=wp), private :: dtout integer, private :: i integer, private :: op type( diag_spec_t ), private, allocatable :: specs (:) Source Code subroutine apply_diag_selection ( state , spec , dt_out , default_coord ) !! Configure the ocean diagnostic set from the unified !! `&ocean_diag_nml diags` selection string.  Single production entry !! point: parses `spec` once, registers the canonical defaults !! (consulting the spec for per-diagnostic `:off` skips and !! `:cadence` / `:op` / `:coord` overrides), then registers any spec !! entries that name a derived-catalog diagnostic (with their overrides). !! !! `default_coord` (a `DIAG_VGRID_*`, default LAYER) is the global !! output vgrid (`&ocean_diag_nml vgrid`) applied to layered diagnostics !! that don't carry a per-diag `:coord`. !! !! An empty / blank `spec` + LAYER default reproduces the canonical set !! exactly (bit-identical).  A spec name that is neither canonical nor !! in the derived catalog fails loud via `register_derived`.  A `:off` !! on a non-canonical name that is not registered is a harmless no-op. !! !! Must be called AFTER the output-level setters (`set_output_z_levels` !! / `set_output_sigma_levels` / `set_output_zstar_levels` / !! `set_output_density_levels`) so non-layer diagnostics size their !! remap targets correctly. type ( ocean_state_t ), intent ( inout ), target :: state character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: spec real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: dt_out integer , intent ( in ), optional :: default_coord type ( diag_spec_t ), allocatable :: specs (:) integer :: i , op , dcoord , coord real ( wp ) :: dtout , dto dtout = 360 0.0_wp if ( present ( dt_out )) dtout = dt_out dcoord = DIAG_VGRID_LAYER if ( present ( default_coord )) dcoord = default_coord specs = parse_diag_spec ( spec ) ! Canonical set, with the spec's per-diagnostic skips / overrides. call register_default_diags ( state , dt_out = dtout , specs = specs , default_coord = dcoord ) ! Derived-catalog additions: any spec entry that is not a canonical ! diagnostic and is not turned off. do i = 1 , size ( specs ) if ( specs ( i )% off ) cycle if ( is_canonical_diag_name ( trim ( specs ( i )% name ))) then if (. not . state % diag % is_registered ( trim ( specs ( i )% name ))) then call global_logger % warning ( & \"&ocean_diag_nml diags requested '\" // trim ( specs ( i )% name ) // & \"', which is a canonical diagnostic but is NOT registered — it will \" // & \"be absent from the output. \" // gate_clause ( trim ( specs ( i )% name ))) end if cycle end if op = DIAG_OP_INSTANT if ( specs ( i )% time_op /= DIAG_OP_UNSET ) op = specs ( i )% time_op dto = dtout if ( specs ( i )% dt_out > 0.0_wp ) dto = specs ( i )% dt_out coord = dcoord if ( specs ( i )% coord /= DIAG_COORD_UNSET ) coord = specs ( i )% coord call register_derived ( state , trim ( specs ( i )% name ), time_op = op , dt_out = dto , coord = coord ) end do end subroutine apply_diag_selection","tags":"","url":"proc/apply_diag_selection.html"},{"title":"fill_h_layer – Roundabout","text":"public  subroutine fill_h_layer(state_handle, buf) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class(*), intent(in) :: state_handle real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: buf (:,:,:) Calls proc~~fill_h_layer~~CallsGraph proc~fill_h_layer fill_h_layer proc~copy3_impl copy3_impl proc~fill_h_layer->proc~copy3_impl Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine fill_h_layer ( state_handle , buf ) class ( * ), intent ( in ) :: state_handle real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: buf (:, :, :) select type ( state => state_handle ) class is ( ocean_state_t ) call copy3_impl ( state % multilayer % h_layer , buf ) end select end subroutine fill_h_layer","tags":"","url":"proc/fill_h_layer.html"},{"title":"fill_ice_speed – Roundabout","text":"public  subroutine fill_ice_speed(state_handle, buf) Sea-ice drift speed |u_ice| at T-centres (m/s) — C-face pairs\naveraged to centre, 2-D twin of the ocean fill_ke stencil.\nIce off / not init ⇒ zeros (never registered by default; opt-in\nvia &ocean_diag_nml diags ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class(*), intent(in) :: state_handle real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: buf (:,:,:) Calls proc~~fill_ice_speed~~CallsGraph proc~fill_ice_speed fill_ice_speed proc~fill_ice_speed_impl fill_ice_speed_impl proc~fill_ice_speed->proc~fill_ice_speed_impl proc~zero3_impl zero3_impl proc~fill_ice_speed->proc~zero3_impl local local proc~fill_ice_speed_impl->local Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine fill_ice_speed ( state_handle , buf ) !! Sea-ice drift speed |u_ice| at T-centres (m/s) — C-face pairs !! averaged to centre, 2-D twin of the ocean `fill_ke` stencil. !! Ice off / not init ⇒ zeros (never registered by default; opt-in !! via `&ocean_diag_nml diags`). class ( * ), intent ( in ) :: state_handle real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: buf (:, :, :) select type ( state => state_handle ) class is ( ocean_state_t ) if (. not . state % ice % is_init ) then call zero3_impl ( buf ) return end if call fill_ice_speed_impl ( state % ice % u_ice , state % ice % v_ice , buf ) end select end subroutine fill_ice_speed","tags":"","url":"proc/fill_ice_speed.html"},{"title":"fill_ice_u – Roundabout","text":"public  subroutine fill_ice_u(state_handle, buf) Eastward sea-ice velocity at T-centres (m/s) — u-face pair\naveraged to centre, 2-D twin of fill_u_centre .  Ice off / not\ninit ⇒ zeros. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class(*), intent(in) :: state_handle real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: buf (:,:,:) Calls proc~~fill_ice_u~~CallsGraph proc~fill_ice_u fill_ice_u proc~fill_ice_u_impl fill_ice_u_impl proc~fill_ice_u->proc~fill_ice_u_impl proc~zero3_impl zero3_impl proc~fill_ice_u->proc~zero3_impl Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows