graphs. Source Code subroutine ocean_data_input_update_2d ( this , id , t , n1 , n2 , dest ) !! Blend field `id`'s current bracket into the caller's WHOLE, !! device-mapped `dest(n1, n2)` array at the registration-time !! offset.  `t` must equal the value `update_all` most recently !! refreshed this field with (fail-loud ordering check — a !! consumer calling this before `update_all` has run for the !! current step is a real bug, not a silent stale read).  Exempt !! for `DATA_TIME_STATIC` fields, whose bracket never changes. class ( ocean_data_input_t ), intent ( in ) :: this integer , intent ( in ) :: id , n1 , n2 real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: dest ( n1 , n2 ) call check_registered ( this , id , is_3d = . false ., n1 = n1 , n2 = n2 ) call check_fresh ( this , id , t ) call data_input_blend_2d_impl ( this % fields ( id )% nx , this % fields ( id )% ny , n1 , n2 , & this % fields ( id )% dest_i0 , this % fields ( id )% dest_j0 , & this % fields ( id )% f0 , this % fields ( id )% f1 , & this % fields ( id )% w , dest ) end subroutine ocean_data_input_update_2d","tags":"","url":"proc/ocean_data_input_update_2d.html"},{"title":"ocean_data_input_update_3d – Roundabout","text":"public  subroutine ocean_data_input_update_3d(this, id, t, n1, n2, n3, dest) 3-D twin of update_2d . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ocean_data_input_t ), intent(in) :: this integer, intent(in) :: id real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: t integer, intent(in) :: n1 integer, intent(in) :: n2 integer, intent(in) :: n3 real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: dest (n1,n2,n3) Calls proc~~ocean_data_input_update_3d~~CallsGraph proc~ocean_data_input_update_3d ocean_data_input_update_3d proc~check_fresh check_fresh proc~ocean_data_input_update_3d->proc~check_fresh proc~check_registered check_registered proc~ocean_data_input_update_3d->proc~check_registered proc~data_input_blend_3d_impl data_input_blend_3d_impl proc~ocean_data_input_update_3d->proc~data_input_blend_3d