des are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code pure function ocean_munk_required_nu_h ( beta , dx , n_cells ) result ( nu_h_req ) !! `nu_h` (m&#94;2/s) needed for `delta_M` to span exactly `n_cells` of !! width `dx` — the audit's suggested fix for a Munk-layer warning. real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: beta , dx , n_cells real ( wp ) :: nu_h_req nu_h_req = beta * ( n_cells * dx ) ** 3 end function ocean_munk_required_nu_h","tags":"","url":"proc/ocean_munk_required_nu_h.html"},{"title":"ocean_viscous_cfl_limit – Roundabout","text":"public pure function ocean_viscous_cfl_limit() result(lim) Accessor for VISCOUS_CFL_LIMIT — tests reference this instead\nof duplicating the literal. Arguments None Return Value real(kind=wp) Source Code pure function ocean_viscous_cfl_limit () result ( lim ) !! Accessor for `VISCOUS_CFL_LIMIT` — tests reference this instead !! of duplicating the literal. real ( wp ) :: lim lim = VISCOUS_CFL_LIMIT end function ocean_viscous_cfl_limit","tags":"","url":"proc/ocean_viscous_cfl_limit.html"},{"title":"ocean_viscous_cfl_max_dt – Roundabout","text":"public pure function ocean_viscous_cfl_max_dt(nu_h, dx_min, limit) result(dt_max) Largest dt (s) that keeps ocean_viscous_cfl_number at or\nbelow limit , at fixed nu_h / dx_min — the “reduce dt below\n…” half of the audit’s suggested fix. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: nu_h real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dx_min real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: limit Return Value real(kind=wp) Called by proc~~ocean_viscous_cfl_max_dt~~CalledByGraph proc~ocean_viscous_cfl_max_dt ocean_viscous_cfl_max_dt proc~ocean_stability_audit ocean_stability_audit proc~ocean_stability_audit->proc~ocean_viscous_cfl_max_dt proc~engine_setup engine_setup proc~engine_setup->proc~ocean_stability_audit proc~complete_ocean_create complete_ocean_create proc~complete_ocean_create->proc~engine_setup proc~driver_run_ocean driver_run_ocean proc~driver_run_ocean->proc~engine_setup proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_ocean proc~rdb_ocean_create_finalize rdb_ocean_create_finalize proc~rdb_ocean_create_finalize->proc~complete_ocean_create proc~rdb_ocean_create_from_string rdb_ocean_create_from_string proc~rdb_ocean_create_from_string->proc~complete_ocean_create Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code pure function ocean_viscous_cfl_max_dt ( nu_h , dx_min , limit ) result ( dt_max ) !! Largest `dt` (s) that keeps `ocean_viscous_cfl_number` at or !! below `limit`, at fixed `nu_h`/`dx_min` — the \"reduce dt below !! ...\" half of the audit's suggested fix. real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: nu_h , dx_min , limit real ( wp ) :: dt_max if ( nu_h > 0.0_wp ) then dt_max = limit * dx_min ** 2 / nu_h else dt_max = huge ( 1.0_wp ) end if end function ocean_viscous_cfl_max_dt","tags":"","url":"proc/ocean_viscous_cfl_max_dt.html"},{"title":"ocean_viscous_cfl_max_nu_h – Roundabout","text":"public pure function ocean_viscous_cfl_max_nu_h(dt, dx_min, limit) result(nu_h_max) Largest nu_h (m&#94;2/s) that keeps ocean_viscous_cfl_number at\nor below limit , at fixed dt / dx_min — the “reduce nu_h\nbelow …” half of the audit’s suggested fix. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dx_min real(kind=wp), intent(in) :