on module imports it);\nignore when developing production code in other modules.\nConvert local physical indices to global physical indices Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( decomp_t ), intent(in) :: d integer, intent(in) :: il Local i-index (1-based, physical cells) integer, intent(in) :: jl Local j-index (1-based, physical cells) integer, intent(out) :: ig Global i-index (1-based, physical cells) integer, intent(out) :: jg Global j-index (1-based, physical cells) public  subroutine decomp_log_summary (d, nprocs) Log the process grid + this rank’s subdomain shape.  Call from\nrank 0 after decomp_init_from_config so a run’s decomposition is\nvisible at startup (the halo perimeter is what auto_factor\nminimises, printed here as the per-rank interior:ghost ratio cue). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( decomp_t ), intent(in) :: d integer, intent(in) :: nprocs Total compute ranks (px*py)","tags":"","url":"module/rdb_decomp.html"},{"title":"rdb_ocean_z_init – Roundabout","text":"Reads pre-regridded T + S from a model-grid NetCDF file\n( &ocean_zinit_nml ), interpolates linearly in depth onto the\nseeded layer-centre depths, and writes the multilayer tracer slots\nas hTr = value * h_layer . File is PRE-REGRIDDED to nx_phys x ny_phys — no in-core\n    horizontal interpolation. Vertical interp is point-linear-in-depth, constant\n    extrapolation beyond the source range. Dry columns ( wet_mask <= 0 ) get the namelist land_fill_t/_s constants. Runs at seed time, HOST-side, BEFORE ocean_state_enter_data , so\nit uses plain host do loops (NOT do concurrent ); the later\nenter_data copies the host-resident arrays up.  NetCDF-only. Uses rdb_grid rdb_ocean_status rdb_io_netcdf rdb_multilayer_state netcdf pic_logger pic_strings rdb_constants rdb_error_ring rdb_config module~~rdb_ocean_z_init~~UsesGraph module~rdb_ocean_z_init rdb_ocean_z_init module~rdb_config rdb_config module~rdb_ocean_z_init->module~rdb_config module~rdb_constants rdb_const