keys (and leave wrote_any). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: unit type( nml_key_box_t ), intent(in) :: box logical, intent(in) :: short_only logical, intent(inout) :: wrote_any","tags":"","url":"module/rdb_nml_schema.html"},{"title":"rdb_ocean_bt_wide – Roundabout","text":"Shadow state for the wide-halo barotropic march-in.\nWhen bt_halo > 0 , the BT fast loop runs on WIDE arrays with ghost\nwidth ng_wide = nghost + bt_halo .  Ghost cells outside the valid\nband evolve stale data that creeps INWARD at 2 cells/substep; one\ngrouped exchange every bt_halo/2 substeps keeps the physical interior\nclean.  The mid-substep u exchange is absorbed (within the 2-cell/substep\nstencil budget). Lifecycle:\n  1. init — allocate wide arrays + wide grid/metrics/f_corner.\n  2. enter_data — attach all wide arrays to the GPU present table.\n  3. Per outer step: copy_in -> (entry_exchange + substep) -> copy_out -> normal-width exit exchange (in the caller).\n  4. exit_data — release GPU present table entries.\n  5. destroy — free host memory. Uses rdb_grid rdb_mem_report rdb_barotropic_substep pic_logger rdb_ocean_boundary_types rdb_constants rdb_barotropic_workstate rdb_ocean_halo rdb_ocean_metrics iso_fortran_env rdb_profiler module~~rdb_ocean_bt_wide~~UsesGraph module~rdb_ocean_bt_wide rdb_ocean_bt_wide iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~rdb_ocean_bt_wide->iso_fortran_env module~rdb_barotropic_substep rdb_barotropic_substep module~rdb_ocean_bt_wide->module~rdb_barotropic_substep module~rdb_barotropic_workstate rdb_barotropic_workstate module~rdb_ocean_bt_wide->module~rdb_barotropic_workstate module~rdb_constants rdb_constants module~rdb_ocean_bt_wide->module~rdb_constants module~rdb_grid rdb_grid module~rdb_ocean_bt_wide->module~rdb_grid module~rdb_mem_report rdb_mem_report module~rdb_ocean_bt_wide->module~rdb_mem_report module~rdb_ocean_boundary_types rdb_ocean_boundary_types module~rdb_ocean_bt_wide->module~rdb_ocean_boundary_types module